    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lēnuncŭlus</span></b> ,
			i, m.
		dim.
		for lembunculus, from lembus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small sailingvessel, a bark, skiff</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pauci lenunculi conveniebant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 2, 43</span></i>
			: in lenunculo piscantes, Sall. Fragm. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 534, 32</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occursu lenunculorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					14, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">piscatorius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 2, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
